title: CafeteriaDay1Afternoon
---
<<declare $Shelly_lieThatSheIsClose = false>>
<<declare $Jerome_isCreative = false>>
<<declare $Jerome_isArtistic = false>>

<<if $Shelly_inviteToLunch>>
    Shelly: Hey, took you long enough. Who's this?
    Me: Oh, he is Marvin. He's my classmate.
    Marvin: Hello, uhh you are?
    Shelly: Shelly! Nice to meet you.
    Shelly: I'm Jerome's highschool friend.
    Marvin: Ahh i see, Were you two close?
    -> Yeah, we were!
        <<set $Shelly_lieThatSheIsClose = true>>
        <<set $Shelly_honestPoint -= 1>>
        Shelly: No, we weren't.
        <<if !$Shelly_knowingHerName>>
            Shelly: Dude, you didn't even remember my name.
        <<endif>>
    -> Not really!
        <<set $Shelly_honestPoint += 1>>
        Shelly: Yeah, you got that right.
        <<if $Shelly_honestPoint >= 2>>
            <<set $Shelly_likePoint += 1>>
            Shelly: Although I regret not at least try to be close.
            Shelly: You're kinda alright.
        <<endif>>
    -> *Says nothing!*
        Shelly: No, we weren't very close.
    <<if $Shelly_lieThatSheIsClose>>
        Marvin: Ok, that's awkward.
        <<if $Marvin_quirkPoint >= 1>>
            Marvin: I'm sure that he just has a hazy memory.
        <<endif>>
    <<else>>
        Marvin: Well, that's interesting.
    <<endif>>
    Marvin: Anyways, i feel like we should get lunch now.
    Marvin: We only have about half an hour left before class starts again.
    Me: Yeah, you're right. Let's go then.
    <<if $Shelly_lieThatSheIsClose>>
        Shelly: Psh, fine.
    <<else>>
        Shelly: Yep, alright.
    <<endif>>
    <<if $Marvin_quirkPoint >= 1>>
        Marvin: I take dibs on the seat next to you Jerome.
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    Marvin: Looks like it's just me and you, huh?
    Me: Yep, just us!
    Marvin: I'm curious, what makes you joining art class?
    -> Because I just love creating.
        <<set $Jerome_isCreative = true>>
        Marvin: I see. So, you're a creative type of person.
        Marvin: I guess we're kinda different.
        Me: Oh how?
    -> Because I feel like art helps me describe myself.
        <<set $Jerome_isArtistic = true>>
        Marvin: I see. So, you're an artistic type of person.
        Marvin: I guess I could say I'm similar to you as well.
        Me: Oh really?
    Marvin: Well, back when I was a kid, I used to draw...a lot
    Marvin: And it was really bad, I swear to god.
    Marvin: But it helped me through tough times.
    <<if $Marvin_quirkPoint >= 1>>
        Marvin: I used to be a bad grade student.
        Marvin: My dad would often told me how drawings would not help my future.
        Marvin: And that I should study more instead.
        Marvin: I listened though and studied Computer Science full time after I graduated.
        Marvin: But then I found about Game Development.
        Marvin: So I decided to take this class as well to improve my artistic side.
        Me: Oh I see. I guess we are similar with parents not wanting us to pursue art.
        -> But I'm glad we both make it through.
            <<set $Marvin_likePoint+= 1>>
        -> But I'm proud that you are able to go through it.
            <<set $Marvin_lovePoint += 1>>
        Marvin: Hehe, yeah. Thanks for listen.
    <<else>>
        Me: Ahh I see, I understand that feeling.
    <<endif>>
    Marvin: Anyways, enough with the heavy topic.
    Marvin: We should grab lunch quick since we only have half an hour left before class.
    Me: Ok, let's go then.
<<endif>>
<<play_crossfade_normal>>
<<change_objective "Go to Art Classroom">>
<<set_object_inactive Afternoon_Marvin2 false>>
<<if $Shelly_inviteToLunch>>
    <<set_object_inactive Afternoon_Shelly false>>
<<endif>>
<<set_object_active "Afternoon_Art_Class_Interact_Point" true>>
===
